From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a <webview> paused on a dialog does not slow the
 shell

A <webview>'s page embeds with the default deadline whenever its visual
properties change, so the shell's frame waits for the page to draw. Two
change every frame of an animation: the part of the frame on screen
(`compositor_viewport`), as a window slides across a screen's edge in a
workspace switch, and its scale (the raster scale and its size in the local root), as a
window grows or shrinks.
A page paused on `alert()`, `confirm()` or `prompt()` draws nothing, so
each frame of the shell waited out the deadline: the switch ran at a
third of its frame rate.

- A <webview> rasters its whole page, so its compositing rect no longer
  follows the screen's edge.
- A change of scale alone embeds with deadline 0: the page's latest
  frame is right, only less sharp until the page draws again.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on crux.
